  "articleBody": "Choosing the right stain for your log home can feel a bit overwhelming, but it's really about understanding what works best for logs. Many people wonder if clear finishes are enough, but here's the thing: clear coats alone aren't usually going to give you the protection you need, especially in sunny Colorado. Darker pigmented stains actually offer more UV protection and durability than clear options. You really want to look for stain systems that are specifically designed for log homes. These aren't your typical deck stains! They're formulated to allow the wood to 'breathe' while still protecting it from moisture and UV rays. When you're cleaning your logs annually, you should also be inspecting them for any peeling stain. If you've got peeling happening, or if you're seeing widespread checking in the logs, it might be time to consider a professional opinion. We can help assess the situation and recommend the best stain system to keep your log home looking great and protected for years to come.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}